course: dictionary
lesson: 12567
title: Words that grow bigger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dilate is a verb. It means to become wider or bigger, especially an opening in the body. Read the words around it for clues. «In the dark, her pupils dilated so more light could get in.» Pupils getting bigger in the dark is the clue, so dilate means to get wider.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «In the dark, her pupils got wider so more light could get in.» It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Dilate changes its ending: dilates, dilated and dilating. «The blood vessels dilated when Sam got hot in the sun.» The -ed ending tells you it has already happened, and the clue hot sun tells you why.
fact: Dilate means to become wider or bigger.
fact: «Dilated pupils» means the black centres of your eyes have grown wider.
fact: Your pupils dilate in dim light so more light can come in, and they shrink in bright light.
fact: «Blood vessels dilate» when you are hot, so more blood can flow near your skin.
fact: In maths, «dilation» means making a shape bigger or smaller by a scale factor. Dilate can also mean to talk or write at length, but this is formal and rare.
exercise: «In the dark, her pupils dilated.» What does dilated mean? | *Became wider | Closed tightly | Turned a different colour | Went to sleep
exercise: «The doctor put drops in my eyes to dilate my pupils.» What does dilate mean here? | To wash the eyes | To read the eye chart | *To make the pupils wider | To close the eyes
exercise: Which word means the same as dilate? | Close | *Widen | Hide | Shrink
test: «Cats' pupils dilate in the dark.» When do their pupils get bigger? | In the bath | In bright sunshine | At school | *In the dark
test: What does dilation mean in maths? | Adding two numbers together | Drawing a circle with a ruler | *Making a shape bigger or smaller by a scale factor | Counting the sides of a shape
exam: Sam says dilate means the same as shrink. Why is he wrong? | Dilate is a noun for a small room | *Shrink means get smaller, but dilate means get wider or bigger | Both words mean the same thing | Dilate means to shrink
